<title>NETHERLANDS: Martinair acquires stakes in Colombian airline.</title>
<headline>Martinair acquires stakes in Colombian airline.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Martinair Holland said on Wednesday it was taking a 40 percent stake in Colombian airline company Tampa.</p>
<p>Martinair said it had also acquired 10 percent of Florida- based Martin Aviation Group (MAG), a cargo sales and services representative for South America.</p>
<p>&quot;Both acquisitions strengthen the position of Martinair in the South American market...,&quot; it said in a statement.</p>
<p>No financial details were given for either deal.</p>
<p>Martinair is jointly owned by KLM Royal Dutch Airlines NV and Nedlloyd.</p>
